# QGIS Visualisation

QGIS was used to visualise and validate the spatial results produced in PostgreSQL/PostGIS.

The main spatial processing and area calculations were performed in PostGIS. QGIS was primarily used for cartographic presentation, layer inspection and final map export.

## PostgreSQL Connection

QGIS was connected directly to the PostgreSQL/PostGIS database.

Important spatial tables and views used during mapping included:

```text
ssa_countries
ssa_boundary
ssa_protected_areas
ssa_protected_coverage
species_protection_map
species_protection_gaps
country_protection_map
